WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.762
Three severities, three meanings,
and they're the kit's design.

2
00:00:03.762 --> 00:00:05.475
A Finding fails the check.

3
00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:08.871
A Warn needs a person to look,
but isn't a failure: here,

4
00:00:08.871 --> 00:00:12.429
a block that's off inside an
approved matching window,

5
00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:15.987
which the run's options record
as the window's last day.

6
00:00:15.987 --> 00:00:21.251
The day after, the same state is a Finding
again, without anyone editing anything.

7
00:00:21.251 --> 00:00:26.461
An Info row gives context and isn't counted:
soft match on U P N, which Microsoft

8
00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:31.838
Learn's Set Entra Dir Sync Feature page
says can't be turned off once it's enabled.

9
00:00:31.838 --> 00:00:35.693
The status comes from the rows:
Fail if there's any Finding,

10
00:00:35.693 --> 00:00:38.237
else Warn if there's any Warn, else Pass.

11
00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:42.150
And the most important rule: a
missing value is read as off.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:47.250
So a response shape the kit doesn't expect
produces a Finding, not a silent Pass.

13
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.750
Default every "is the control
on" read to the unsafe answer.

14
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:56.400
NotApplicable is for a tenant with
nothing to check, never for a failed read.
